  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can I read fuel level remotely on a Chevrolet Malibu?",
      "a": "Yes, with a DIMO device. Query the powertrainFuelSystemRelativeLevel signal through the Telemetry API, and use segments with the refuel mechanism to find where fuel level rises significantly."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I track a Chevrolet Malibu with no connected services?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device. After the owner shares the vehicle with your app, exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT through the Token Exchange API, then query the Telemetry API."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I get check-engine light alerts for a Chevrolet Malibu?",
      "a": "Yes, the DIMO LTE R1 device lists the dtc event for this model, along with the obdDTCList and obdStatusDTCCount signals. Use the Vehicle Triggers API (webhooks) to have DIMO push alerts to your server, so you don't have to poll."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on a Chevrolet Malibu?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device, which both listed devices support for idling. Call the segments query in the Telemetry API with the idling mechanism, which returns periods where engine RPM stays in the idle range."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Chevrolet Malibu mileage?",
      "a": "Read the odometer from a DIMO device, then call the Attestation API odometer-statement endpoint with a Vehicle JWT. It generates a verifiable odometer attestation that you retrieve through the Telemetry API."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO gives developers API access to vehicle-state data: diagnostics, fault codes, battery and fuel health, odometer, and maintenance signals. For the Chevrolet Malibu, data comes from a DIMO device, for 2010 and newer model years. This coverage has been tested rather than only expected. Query the Telemetry API with a Vehicle JWT to read the signals the vehicle reports."
